libimud (1.10.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * imud builds and runs on big-endian hosts. The binary packet and the
    .imucap file are converted field by field instead of memcpy'd in host
    order, so they stay little-endian whatever the machine, and the Debian
    packages are now Architecture: linux-any.  No wire-format change of
    its own: the bytes a little-endian host emits are identical to before.
    The packet does move to v18 in this release, for a separate change.
  * Wire format v18: the packet grows 276 to 288 bytes with flags_ext, a
    second 32-bit flag word, and eight reserved bytes. Every existing
    field keeps its offset. Its first bit says no magnetometer is
    configured.  Breaking: consumers reject a wire version they do not
    know, so deploy the daemon and its consumers together. flags had
    assigned all sixteen bits, which is what forced the new word — a
    consumer must ignore bits it does not recognise, and a later flag then
    needs no further bump. The imud-arduino client needs its own update.
  * The packet's fifo_overflow flag (bit 7) is now actually set when
    samples are lost, and the daemon logs the gap at 1 Hz saying whether
    the hardware FIFO overflowed or the internal ring dropped.  The bit
    has been documented since the format was first published and was never
    raised, so no consumer could detect a sample gap; only imud-status's
    counter showed one, and not when it happened. It is latched for about
    two seconds so a slow consumer still sees it.
  * The armhf packages are now built on Raspbian at the ARMv6 baseline, so
    they run on every Raspberry Pi that boots a 32-bit userland.
    Previously they were built to Debian's ARMv7 baseline.  On a Pi 1 or
    Pi Zero/Zero W the previous packages installed without complaint and
    then died on an illegal instruction, because both ports report the
    same "armhf" architecture. Those boards can now install from the apt
    repository. The arm64 packages are unchanged.

 -- Richard Simpson <richcreations@gmail.com>  Sat, 05 Sep 2026 09:31:46 -0700

libimud (1.9.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * An uncalibrated magnetometer is now fused for heading instead of
    ignored. Heading is offset by the uncorrected hard iron but bounded,
    where before it dead-reckoned without bound. Heading-only, so roll and
    pitch are untouched, and withdrawn automatically under gross iron.
    New flag bit 15, FLAG_MAG_UNCAL, marks the uncalibrated-but-fused
    state. FLAG_MAG_VALID is unchanged and still means calibrated and
    healthy, so existing consumers need no change. The wire packet is
    byte-identical and still v17. This spends the last free flag bit. Set
    mag_fuse_uncal = false to restore the old behaviour.  ACTION: Run
    imud-cal mag for a heading accurate enough to navigate on; this is a
    floor, not a substitute.

 -- Richard Simpson <richcreations@gmail.com>  Mon, 31 Aug 2026 16:57:43 -0700

libimud (1.9.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * imud.h documents ts_wall_ns correctly: it carries the instant the
    SENSOR sampled, reconstructed from the chip counter, not the moment
    the packet was sent. The old comment, "CLOCK_REALTIME, nanoseconds",
    read as emit time and hid the two things the field is for --
    correlating an imud sample with another sensor, and computing
    end-to-end age as now() - ts_wall_ns at receipt. The field itself is
    unchanged.
  * No ABI change: imud_data_t is untouched, libimud.map has not grown,
    and the SONAME stays libimud.so.0.

 -- Richard Simpson <richcreations@gmail.com>  Mon, 10 Aug 2026 04:48:20 -0700

libimud (1.8.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New flag bit IMUD_FLAG_STATE_RESET (1u << 14), in imud.h, the
    standalone imud_client.h and imud_client.py alike: the daemon's MEKF
    found a non-finite value in its own state and reset itself. It is
    latched from the reset until the filter re-converges rather than
    being a single-packet pulse, so a consumer polling well below the
    packet rate can still see it, and IMUD_FLAG_FUSION_CONVERGED is
    clear for the same span. The Python client renders it as R in
    Flags.describe().
  * No ABI change and no wire-format change. imud_data_t is untouched,
    lib/libimud.map is unchanged, the SONAME stays libimud.so.0, and the
    packet stays v17 / 276 bytes — bit 14 was reserved and simply gained
    a meaning, so a consumer built against 1.8.1 needs no rebuild.

 -- Richard Simpson <richcreations@gmail.com>  Wed, 05 Aug 2026 12:00:00 -0700

libimud (1.8.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Harden: the socket imud_open() creates is now close-on-exec, so a
    consumer that forks and execs no longer leaks its imud socket into
    the child. Taken atomically via SOCK_CLOEXEC where the platform has
    it. The macro is kept inline rather than shared with the rest of the
    tree because this header must compile standalone against nothing but
    libc, which is the point of it.
  * Documented: IMUD_VERSION in the Python client is the wire-layout
    revision, NOT the release version — it is 17 because 1.7 was the
    release that last changed the packet layout, and a 1.8 daemon still
    speaks 17. The C headers already said so; the Python one did not, so
    a consumer read it as stale and went looking for a protocol change
    that never happened. CI now checks the constant agrees across
    include/types.h, lib/imud_client.h and lib/imud_client.py.
  * No ABI change: imud_data_t is unchanged and the SONAME stays
    libimud.so.0. Existing binaries do not need recompiling.

 -- Richard Simpson <richcreations@gmail.com>  Mon, 03 Aug 2026 12:00:00 -0700

libimud (1.7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * imud_data_t gains the wire-v17 MEKF diagnostic fields (append-only,
    ABI preserved): innov_weight and innov_reject report how hard the
    filter is having to distrust its sensors, nis_accel and nis_mag
    report whether the noise model itself is right (1.0 = the filter's
    covariance is consistent with the innovations it sees, higher means
    over-confident). Existing binaries keep working unchanged and do not
    need recompiling; the SONAME stays libimud.so.0.
  * Documented: the Euler attitude fields (pitch, roll, yaw, heading_deg,
    rate_of_turn) are ZYX intrinsic angles and are singular at pitch
    +/-90 deg by construction. Consumers that can encounter steep pitch
    must read quat_*, which is never singular. No code change — the
    quaternion has always been there.

 -- Richard Simpson <richcreations@gmail.com>  Mon, 27 Jul 2026 12:00:00 -0700

libimud (1.6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New imud_connect_tcp(host, port): connect to a daemon's [stream] TCP
    listener ([stream] tcp_enabled, default port 10112) for the same
    lossless framed packets as imud_connect_stream, over the network.
    Additive — new symbol version node IMUD_1; the SONAME stays
    libimud.so.0 and existing binaries are unaffected.

 -- Richard Simpson <richcreations@gmail.com>  Sun, 19 Jul 2026 12:00:00 -0700

libimud (1.5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * imud_data_t.temp_c now carries the real IMU die temperature — the daemon
    never enabled FIFO temperature batching before 1.5, so the field was a
    25.0 degC placeholder in every prior release. No API/ABI change.

